  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Crop production and livestock health and productivity support</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: Emergency crop production and livelihoods protected through rapid delivery of inputs, small equipment, and cash assistance to vulnerable households in frontline areas.
Activities:
- Provide seeds to rural households
- Vouchers/greenhouses for SAR-registered households
- Vouchers for small-scale farmers, soil conservation support
- Demonstration plots for soil/crop risk mitigation
- Cash for IDPs to restore crop production

Output: Livestock health and productivity are safeguarded through integrated protection measures, including early identification of threats and risks, proactive mitigation actions, and timely provision of emergency support packages to vulnerable households
Activities:
- Cash + poultry kits to rural households
- Cash for animal feed to livestock-owning households
- Cash for IDPs to restore livestock production

Each component is guided by clear indicators and measurable targets, enabling data-driven monitoring and adaptive management to ensure responsiveness to evolving security and environmental conditions.

The project is based on a gender sensitive approach and data are collected disaggregated by gender, age and disability, ensuring gender-sensitive and inclusive access to financial services.</narrative>
  </description>
